      "writtenOn": "2018-09-26T09:32:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a no-op if mMtu is null. For consistency with the code above, I think we should let that method check for nullity.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 722,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 722,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "a9d221c588103641b6947a2766e97efbd5cedf7c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0c560aa4_33944f0c",
        "filename": "services/net/java/android/net/dhcp/DhcpPacket.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 722,
      "author": {
        "id": 1288034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-09-27T02:31:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "However I can\u0027t just remove the null check since I\u0027d get a NPE when unboxing mMtu to compare with 0; I could use (mMtu \u003d\u003d null || mMtu !\u003d 0) but that doesn\u0027t look very good.\nI could also have a addTlvIfNonZero() method, but I\u0027d be adding some duplicate code. Do you have other options in mind ?",
      "parentUuid": "2533938a_4c94b174",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 722,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 722,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "a9d221c588103641b6947a2766e97efbd5cedf7c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "41347728_ecf89af8",
        "filename": "services/net/java/android/net/dhcp/DhcpPacket.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 722,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-09-28T13:44:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is always the option of changing mMtu from a Short to a short. It does look to me like this class is treating them as equivalent, though I understand that morally they aren\u0027t. RFC2132 also says the minimum legal value for this field is 68, so I\u0027m not sure why you special case 0 (instead of, say, \u003e\u003d 68).\n\nBut I don\u0027t have a strong opinion either way.",
      "parentUuid": "0c560aa4_33944f0c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 722,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 722,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "a9d221c588103641b6947a2766e97efbd5cedf7c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1fc7fb12_bd979ca2",
        "filename": "services/net/java/android/net/dhcp/DhcpPacket.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 722,
      "author": {
        "id": 1288034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-01T02:14:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Changing it to a short would be a good option, although if I want to keep consistency I might want to also change the other members (mLeaseTime, mT1, mT2, mMaxMessageSize etc) - I\u0027ll keep it nullable for now though, to keep the change simple.\nGood point about 0 vs. \u003e\u003d 68: changed to check that the value is greater than that.",
      "parentUuid": "41347728_ecf89af8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 722,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 722,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "a9d221c588103641b6947a2766e97efbd5cedf7c",
